2026-09-04T07:49Z claude note AUTHOR RULING: A CLEAN TEST SUITE IS NOT VALIDATION. Asked whether wiring the missing perturbation would both close gap C locally and validate the staged upstream counters PR for sending, the author corrected the framing: 0642's counters PR passing its own full test suite (1097 tests, lint/build/typecheck clean) proves the patch is CORRECT, not that it solves the problem it was built for. The bar for sending anything upstream is higher -- prove it actually unblocks the downstream need first. Filed as tickets/0643 (Ticket-ref this ticket, 0642, 0033 -- closes none): wire the build-triggered perturbation, get a real local PASS/FAIL on both R22 clauses against the 0642-patched build, and only THEN is the upstream PR considered validated -- the send decision still waits on the author regardless of outcome. This is now the standing bar for any prepared artifact this project sends outward: green tests are necessary, not sufficient; run the check it exists to unblock before proposing to send it.
