2026-09-04T08:50Z claude note GAP C'S CAUSE SENT UPSTREAM, on the author's explicit go-ahead, framed as a soft proposal (not a demand -- current behavior is reasonable for the common case and may be intentional) matching #54's shape: oscardvs/zoteus#56 (https://github.com/oscardvs/zoteus/issues/56), "Stopping a build doesn't keep it paused." Two shapes offered, neither demanded: a persisted paused flag build/update check against, or a distinct resume action separate from build's resume/rebuild/repair overload. Ticket 0644 (filed and closed same action). This does not move R22 -- stays FAIL, correctly, until the maintainer ships something and it is re-measured against a real build carrying both 0642's counters and whatever he builds (the author's own directed next step, once there is something to re-measure against). verification/UPSTREAM-PR-WORK-COUNTERS-0642.md stays unsent. SYNC.md's tracker table carries the filing.
