| 0636 | gap C — an R22-only check via a new perturbation and a direct sqlite read, independent of 0033/0032 | filed 2026-09-04, closed same day: author declined (high road) — see log |
| 0642 | gap C — phased Tier-2 counters design; Phase 0+1 (durable embed-stage counter) is the goal-1 slice, phases 2-4 stay 0033's | filed 2026-09-04, Phase 0+1 implemented and merged (PR #345) — real, durable, tests green, but R22 still not-run: counters were necessary, not sufficient, see 0643 |
| 0643 | gap C — wire a build-triggered perturbation into durability.py, the missing half of R22; also the author-directed validation gate the upstream counters PR must clear before it can be considered for sending | filed 2026-09-04, closed same day (PR #347): counter/perturbation execution proven; its explicit-build FAILs reclassified as non-verdict evidence by the 0665 audit |
| 0644 | gap C — file the pause-shape observation upstream | filed and closed 2026-09-04: sent as oscardvs/zoteus#56; the filing stands as an observation, not a faithful R22 verdict |
